Mostly it will unify logging across all code, every module just own a logger with name so you dont need to write categories in outputs. Mostly every plugin has this: 
`    if (const char* env_p = std::getenv("MAVSDK_CAMERA_DEBUGGING")) {
        if (std::string(env_p) == "1") {
            LogDebug("Camera debugging is on.");
            _debugging = true;
        }
    }`

which can be simplified to `camera_log = std::make_shared<spdlog::logger>("camera", sink); camera_log->info("Connected")` where spdlog will read env variable at startup which looks like this: `SPDLOG_LEVEL="network=debug,camera=warn"` or `export SPDLOG_LEVEL="info"` so no need that messy many env variables. Also you can provide sinks instead of `mavsdk::log::subscribe`. 
There are many other features that you can find helpful...
